Package: epidemiologysuite
Title: Sample Size, Power and Analysis Tools for Epidemiology
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Mukul", "Maheshwari", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "ryan00700@gmail.com")
Description: A 'shiny' application and a set of R functions that help
    choose a study design and calculate the sample size or power for about
    160 designs (proportions, means, diagnostic accuracy, agreement,
    observational studies, clinical trials, survival, prediction models,
    cluster and multilevel designs, general statistical tests and more), with
    tools for analysing summary data (2 x 2 tables, rates, Mantel-Haenszel and
    standardization, vaccine efficacy, outbreak measures, aberration
    detection), drawing survey samples and randomization lists. Every
    calculator shows its formula, a worked example and a citable source, and
    results can be exported as a methods-section paragraph, CSV, JSON, BibTeX
    or RIS. Calculations are closed-form or simulation-based and are
    cross-checked against established R packages.
